## Travel-router notes

When the admin Mac is on a non-home subnet (e.g. travel router):

- mDNS (`*.local`) often fails even if home gateway unicast works.
- Prefer short alias (`ssh moon`) which uses `HostName` IP.
- Primary Mac’s own home reservation may not answer until that interface is on home LAN.
